/ A typed list holds its element type: what goes in stays as it came, and each element is born a path at its own
/ first read, never left as text.
Start
- set %files% as list of path = ["a.txt", "b.txt"]
- assert %files!type.name% equals "list"
- assert %files[0]!type.name% equals "path", "each element is born as the element type of the list"
